    "title": "PLAY TEAMSHEET: Can YOU name the Crystal Palace team that put five past Newcastle in 2015?",
    "text": "By Lewis Browning\nPublished: 07:03 GMT, February 9, 2025 | Updated: 07:03 GMT, February 9, 2025\nWelcome to the team sheet again … Mail Sport’s original soccer game with a turn that gives you the opportunity to try your knowledge of football against your classmates.\nToday, we want to see if you can name the Crystal Palace team that went to five beyond Newcastle in November 2015, surpassing the Magpies 5-1. It was a very different side of Newcastle at that time, under a different property, but they were the second best in Selhurst Park while the hosts ran disturbances.\nIt is only for fun, so see how you go and share the score of your team sheet … The complete instructions on how to play are at the bottom of the article and in the game itself.\nBest of luck!\nHow to play The goal of the game is to write down as many points as possible!\nIf you guess a player in the first attempt, you write down a point, so the lowest score to guess each player in the first attempt is 11.\nGuess a correct letter in the correct position, and will become green. Guess a correct letter but in the wrong position, and it will become yellow.\nYou have six conjectures for each player, and if you fail, we will reveal their identity for 11 points! You can also request a free letter, but it costs you a point.\nSo play to see if he gets the best total possible of 11, or fails in each player and scores 121.\nShare or comment on this article: Play Team sheet: Can you name the Crystal Palace team that passed five beyond Newcastle in 2015?\n(Tagstotranslate) Dailymail (T) Sport (T) Team leaf",
